          The gap between a $4,000 zero turn and a $15,000 one is not the engine. It is what drives the wheels, how thick the deck steel is, and how many hours the warranty is written for. Get those three right and nearly any machine on this list will outlast the crew running it; get them wrong and you will be shopping again in three seasons.
